# odd-board environment variables
#
# Copy this file to .env and fill in the values you need:
#   cp .env.example .env
# .env is gitignored and never committed. This file is committed and lists
# every variable without real values.
#
# Keep both files in sync: when code, a script or tooling starts reading a
# variable, add it here in the same commit (name, safe default or empty,
# what reads it, whether it is required). test/env-example.test.js fails if
# bin/ or src/ reads a process.env variable that is not listed here.
#
# Node does not load .env by itself. Use: node --env-file=.env bin/odd-board.js
# (Node 20.6 or later).

# --- Runtime -----------------------------------------------------------------
# odd-board reads no environment variables today. Everything is configured
# with CLI flags (see `odd-board --help`).

# --- CI secrets (GitHub repository secrets, not set here) --------------------
# npm publishing needs none: .github/workflows/release.yml uses trusted
# publishing (OIDC), so no token is stored. See docs/releasing.md.
#
# SITE_DEPLOY_KEY: private half of a read-only deploy key on the private
# repository claudiocebpaz/odd-board-site. Read by .github/workflows/site.yml to
# build and deploy the website. Required for the website only. Set by the owner,
# never here. See docs/website.md.
# SITE_DEPLOY_KEY=
